{
  "permissions": {
    "defaultMode": "acceptEdits",
    "deny": [
      "Bash(rm -rf /)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf ~)",
      "Bash(rm -rf ~/*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /publicfs/*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /workfs*)",
      "Bash(sudo *)",
      "Bash(:(){ :|:& };:)",
      "Bash(chmod -R 000 *)",
      "Bash(chmod -R 777 *)",
      "Bash(chown *)",
      "Bash(git push --force * master)",
      "Bash(git push --force * main)",
      "Bash(git push -f * master)",
      "Bash(git push -f * main)",
      "Bash(git reset --hard HEAD~*)",
      "Bash(git clean -fd)",
      "Bash(* | xargs rm *)",
      "Bash(* | xargs rm)",
      "Bash(find * -delete)",
      "Bash(find * -exec rm *)",
      "Bash(* && rm -rf *)",
      "Bash(* && sudo *)",
      "Bash(* && chmod -R 000 *)",
      "Bash(* && chmod -R 777 *)",
      "Bash(* && chown *)",
      "Bash(* && git push --force *)",
      "Bash(* && git push -f *)",
      "Bash(* && git reset --hard *)",
      "Bash(* && git clean -fd)",
      "Bash(* && find * -delete)",
      "Bash(* && * | xargs rm)",
      "Bash(rm * && *)",
      "Bash(sudo * && *)",
      "Write(/publicfs/cms/data/**)",
      "Edit(/publicfs/cms/data/**)",
      "Write(/etc/**)",
      "Edit(/etc/**)",
      "Write(/usr/**)",
      "Edit(/usr/**)",
      "Write(~/.ssh/**)",
      "Edit(~/.ssh/**)"
    ],
    "allow": [
      "Bash(*)",
      "Edit(*)",
      "Write(*)",
      "Read(*)",
      "Glob(**)",
      "Grep(**)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "userPromptSubmit": {
      "command": "bash",
      "args": [".claude/hooks/user-prompt-submit.sh"],
      "env": {
        "USER_PROMPT": "{{user_prompt}}",
        "PROJECT_ROOT": "{{project_root}}"
      }
    },
    "preToolUse": {
      "command": "bash",
      "args": [".claude/hooks/pre-tool-use.sh"],
      "env": {
        "TOOL_NAME": "{{tool_name}}",
        "BASH_COMMAND": "{{bash_command}}",
        "PROJECT_ROOT": "{{project_root}}"
      }
    },
    "postToolUse": {
      "command": "bash",
      "args": [".claude/hooks/post-tool-use.sh"],
      "env": {
        "TOOL_NAME": "{{tool_name}}",
        "FILE_PATH": "{{file_path}}",
        "PROJECT_ROOT": "{{project_root}}"
      }
    }
  },
  "codeQuality": {
    "python": {
      "maxFunctionLines": 80,
      "recommendedFunctionLines": 50,
      "maxNestingDepth": 5,
      "recommendedNestingDepth": 3,
      "maxBranches": 20,
      "recommendedBranches": 10,
      "maxFileLines": 1000,
      "recommendedFileLines": 500
    },
    "cpp": {
      "maxFunctionLines": 150,
      "maxFileLines": 800
    }
  },
  "comments": [
    "=== UPDATED 2025-12-11: Deny-list approach for zero prompts ===",
    "",
    "STRATEGY: Deny-List Approach (Simplified)",
    "  - Allow everything by default: Bash(*), Edit(*), Write(*), Read(*), Glob(**), Grep(**)",
    "  - Explicit deny rules block dangerous operations only",
    "  - Zero prompts for normal workflow commands",
    "  - Maximum flexibility with safety guarantee",
    "",
    "DENY RULES (Priority: Blocks dangerous operations):",
    "  - System-wide deletions: rm -rf /, /publicfs/*, /workfs*, ~/*",
    "  - Sudo commands: elevation to root",
    "  - Fork bombs and malicious patterns",
    "  - Destructive permission changes: chmod -R 000/777, chown",
    "  - Force-pushing to main/master branches",
    "  - Hard git resets and aggressive cleanup: git reset --hard, git clean -fd",
    "  - Piped deletions: | xargs rm, find -delete, find -exec rm",
    "  - Compound dangerous operations:",
    "    - * && rm -rf *, * && sudo *, * && chmod -R 000/777 *",
    "    - * && git push --force *, * && git reset --hard *",
    "    - rm * && *, sudo * && * (dangerous commands first in chain)",
    "  - Writing to system directories: /etc/**, /usr/**, ~/.ssh/**",
    "  - Writing to read-only NanoAOD data: /publicfs/cms/data/**",
    "",
    "ALLOW RULES (Everything else):",
    "  - Bash(*) - All bash commands except explicitly denied",
    "  - Edit(*), Write(*), Read(*) - All file operations",
    "  - Glob(**), Grep(**) - All search operations",
    "",
    "SAFETY PHILOSOPHY:",
    "  1. Deny list takes absolute priority - explicitly blocked operations cannot run",
    "  2. Everything else allowed without prompts",
    "  3. Simpler configuration, easier to maintain",
    "  4. Deny rules protect critical system areas and destructive operations",
    "  5. User productivity maximized - no interruptions for safe operations",
    "",
    "HOOKS:",
    "  - userPromptSubmit: Auto-inject workflow context based on keywords",
    "  - preToolUse: Check environment setup before running analysis scripts",
    "  - postToolUse: Code quality checks after Edit/Write operations",
    "  See .claude/hooks/ and .claude/skills/ for implementations"
  ]
}
